IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `aia-core`
IMPORT `aia-timeline`
IMPORT `P9-gate`
IMPORT `P9-art-95-96`

-- Tests for Articles 95 and 96. Expected values are written from the text of the Articles (as enacted and as amended by the
-- Omnibus), Article 113 (group General from 2 August 2026) and the Omnibus's Article 4 (the amended text from 27 July 2026),
-- never copied from the encoding's own output. A dispatcher is asked on 26 July 2026 and 27 July 2026 (each side of the
-- Omnibus) and on 1 and 2 August 2026 (each side of the group's date); the group applies after the Omnibus, so the dispatcher's
-- as-enacted branch is dead, and the as-enacted text is tested through its own function.

§ `Article 95(1)`

-- args: date asked, the codes are intended to foster the voluntary application of Chapter III Section 2 to AI systems other than high-risk
#ASSERT `Art 95(1) the AI Office and the Member States must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(1) the AI Office and the Member States must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(1) the AI Office and the Member States must encourage and facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 95(1) the duty of the AI Office and the Member States to encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 95 the AI Office or a Member State` DOES `Art 95(1) encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct intended to foster the voluntary application of the requirements of Chapter III Section 2` AT 5
-- A duty with no time limit and no stated consequence is never breached: nobody acts, and it stays open.
-- EXPECT PENDING
#TRACE `Art 95(1) the duty of the AI Office and the Member States to encourage and facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

§ `Article 95(2)`

-- args: date asked, the codes concern the voluntary application, including by deployers, of specific requirements to all AI systems
#ASSERT `Art 95(2) the AI Office and the Member States must facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(2) the AI Office and the Member States must facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(2) the AI Office and the Member States must facilitate the drawing up of the codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 95(2) the duty of the AI Office and the Member States to facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 95 the AI Office or a Member State` DOES `Art 95(2) facilitate the drawing up of codes of conduct concerning the voluntary application of specific requirements to all AI systems` AT 5
-- The five named elements are included; "but not limited to" leaves the list open.
#ASSERT `Art 95(2) the element is one the codes of conduct include` `Art 95(2)(a) applicable elements provided for in Union ethical guidelines for trustworthy AI` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(2) the element is one the codes of conduct include` `Art 95(2)(b) assessing and minimising the impact of AI systems on environmental sustainability` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(2) the element is one the codes of conduct include` `Art 95(2)(c) promoting AI literacy` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(2) the element is one the codes of conduct include` `Art 95(2)(d) facilitating an inclusive and diverse design of AI systems` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(2) the element is one the codes of conduct include` `Art 95(2)(e) assessing and preventing the negative impact of AI systems on vulnerable persons or groups of vulnerable persons` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(2) the element is one the codes of conduct include` `Art 95(2) another element` EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 95(3)`

-- args: date asked, the person is an individual provider or deployer, the person is an organisation representing providers or deployers
#ASSERT `Art 95(3) the person may draw up codes of conduct` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(3) the person may draw up codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(3) the person may draw up codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(3) the person may draw up codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(3) the person may draw up codes of conduct` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args: date asked, the number of AI systems the code covers
#ASSERT `Art 95(3) a code of conduct may cover the AI systems` (Date 1 8 2026) 2 EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(3) a code of conduct may cover the AI systems` (Date 2 8 2026) 1 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(3) a code of conduct may cover the AI systems` (Date 2 8 2026) 5 EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(3) a code of conduct may cover the AI systems` (Date 2 8 2026) 0 EQUALS NOTHING

§ `Article 95(4): the text as enacted and as amended`

-- As enacted: SMEs, including start-ups. As amended: and SMCs.
-- args: SME (including a start-up), SMC
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) as enacted the specific interests and needs of the enterprise must be taken into account` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) as enacted the specific interests and needs of the enterprise must be taken into account` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) as amended the specific interests and needs of the enterprise must be taken into account` TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) as amended the specific interests and needs of the enterprise must be taken into account` FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) as amended the specific interests and needs of the enterprise must be taken into account` FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args (dispatcher): date asked, SME (including a start-up), SMC
-- Each side of 27 July 2026: the group does not apply yet, so NOTHING on both.
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) the AI Office and the Member States must take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` (Date 26 7 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) the AI Office and the Member States must take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` (Date 27 7 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) the AI Office and the Member States must take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` (Date 1 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- From 2 August 2026 the text as amended governs: an SMC counts, an SME counts, another enterprise does not.
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) the AI Office and the Member States must take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) the AI Office and the Member States must take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 95(4) the AI Office and the Member States must take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 95(4) the duty of the AI Office and the Member States to take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 95 the AI Office or a Member State` DOES `Art 95(4) take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise when encouraging and facilitating the drawing up of codes of conduct` AT 5
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 95(4) the duty of the AI Office and the Member States to take into account the specific interests and needs of the enterprise` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE FALSE AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

§ `Article 96(1): the topics, as enacted and as amended`

-- As enacted: points (a) to (f), point (a) naming Articles 8 to 15 and Article 25. As amended: also Article 26 in point (a), and point (g).
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the requirements and obligations referred to in Articles 8 to 15` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 25` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 26` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(b) the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(c) the practical implementation of the provisions related to substantial modification` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(d) the practical implementation of transparency obligations laid down in Article 50` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(e) detailed information on the relationship of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, as well as with other relevant Union law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(f) the application of the definition of an AI system as set out in Article 3, point (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1) another topic` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the requirements and obligations referred to in Articles 8 to 15` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 25` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 26` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(b) the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(c) the practical implementation of the provisions related to substantial modification` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(d) the practical implementation of transparency obligations laid down in Article 50` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(e) detailed information on the relationship of this Regulation with the Union harmonisation legislation listed in Annex I, as well as with other relevant Union law` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(f) the application of the definition of an AI system as set out in Article 3, point (1)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1)(g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must develop guidelines on the topic` `Art 96(1) another topic` EQUALS NOTHING
-- args (dispatcher): date asked, the topic. Each side of 27 July 2026 and of 2 August 2026.
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` (Date 26 7 2026) `Art 96(1)(g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` (Date 27 7 2026) `Art 96(1)(g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 96(1)(g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3)` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1)(g) the practical implementation of Article 8(2), Article 9(10) and Article 17(3)` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1)(a) the application of the obligations referred to in Article 26` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1)(b) the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1) another topic` EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 96(1) the duty of the Commission to develop guidelines on the topic` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1)(b) the prohibited practices referred to in Article 5` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 96 the Commission` DOES `Art 96(1) develop guidelines on the practical implementation of this Regulation on the topic` AT 5
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 96(1) the duty of the Commission to develop guidelines on the topic` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1) another topic` AT 0 WITH
    WAITUNTIL 400

§ `Article 96(1)(g): the guidelines shall be published by 1 August 2027`

-- args: date asked, the day from which the time is counted. Counted from 2 August 2026, the guidelines are due by 1 August 2027.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 96(1)(g) the duty of the Commission to publish the guidelines by 1 August 2027` (Date 2 8 2026) (Date 2 8 2026) AT (Day (Date 2 8 2026)) WITH
    PARTY `Art 96 the Commission` DOES `Art 96(1)(g) publish the guidelines on the complementarity and proportionality of the requirements` AT (Day (Date 1 8 2027))
-- Published on the last day: within the time. One day later: BREACH.
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 96(1)(g) the duty of the Commission to publish the guidelines by 1 August 2027` (Date 2 8 2026) (Date 2 8 2026) AT (Day (Date 2 8 2026)) WITH
    PARTY `Art 96 the Commission` DOES `Art 96(1)(g) publish the guidelines on the complementarity and proportionality of the requirements` AT (Day (Date 2 8 2027))
-- EXPECT BREACH
#TRACE `Art 96(1)(g) the duty of the Commission to publish the guidelines by 1 August 2027` (Date 2 8 2026) (Date 2 8 2026) AT (Day (Date 2 8 2026)) WITH
    WAITUNTIL (Day (Date 2 8 2027))
-- Before the group applies (1 August 2026): nothing is owed. Each side of 27 July 2026 (the Omnibus): the group does not apply yet either way.
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 96(1)(g) the duty of the Commission to publish the guidelines by 1 August 2027` (Date 1 8 2026) (Date 1 8 2026) AT (Day (Date 1 8 2026)) WITH
    WAITUNTIL (Day (Date 2 8 2027))
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 96(1)(g) the duty of the Commission to publish the guidelines by 1 August 2027` (Date 26 7 2026) (Date 26 7 2026) AT (Day (Date 26 7 2026)) WITH
    WAITUNTIL (Day (Date 2 8 2027))
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 96(1)(g) the duty of the Commission to publish the guidelines by 1 August 2027` (Date 27 7 2026) (Date 27 7 2026) AT (Day (Date 27 7 2026)) WITH
    WAITUNTIL (Day (Date 2 8 2027))

§ `Article 96(1) second subparagraph: the Board and the beneficiaries`

-- args: the Commission is issuing guidelines under Article 96(1)
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must involve the Board` TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must involve the Board` TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must involve the Board` FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- args (dispatcher): date asked, the Commission is issuing guidelines
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must involve the Board when issuing the guidelines` (Date 27 7 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must involve the Board when issuing the guidelines` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must involve the Board when issuing the guidelines` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must involve the Board when issuing the guidelines` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 96(1) the duty of the Commission to involve the Board when issuing the guidelines` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 96 the Commission` DOES `Art 96(1) involve the Board when issuing the guidelines` AT 5
-- args: the beneficiary
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) SMEs, including start-ups` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) SMCs` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) local public authorities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) the sectors most likely to be affected by this Regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as enacted the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) another beneficiary` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) SMEs, including start-ups` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) SMCs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) local public authorities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) the sectors most likely to be affected by this Regulation` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) as amended the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` `Art 96(1) another beneficiary` EQUALS NOTHING
-- args (dispatcher): date asked, the beneficiary
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines` (Date 27 7 2026) `Art 96(1) SMCs` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines` (Date 1 8 2026) `Art 96(1) SMCs` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1) SMCs` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1) local public authorities` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the Commission must pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1) another beneficiary` EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 96(1) the duty of the Commission to pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary` (Date 2 8 2026) `Art 96(1) SMCs` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 96 the Commission` DOES `Art 96(1) pay particular attention to the needs of the beneficiary when issuing the guidelines` AT 5

§ `Article 96(1) third subparagraph and Article 96(2)`

-- args: date asked, due account of the state of the art, due account of the standards and specifications
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the guidelines take due account of the state of the art and the standards` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the guidelines take due account of the state of the art and the standards` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the guidelines take due account of the state of the art and the standards` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 96(1) the guidelines take due account of the state of the art and the standards` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- args: date asked, guidelines have previously been adopted, the Commission deems the update necessary
#ASSERT `Art 96(2) the Commission must update the guidelines previously adopted` (Date 1 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `Art 96(2) the Commission must update the guidelines previously adopted` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `Art 96(2) the Commission must update the guidelines previously adopted` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST FALSE
#ASSERT `Art 96(2) the Commission must update the guidelines previously adopted` (Date 2 8 2026) FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- EXPECT FULFILLED
#TRACE `Art 96(2) the duty of the Commission to update the guidelines previously adopted` (Date 2 8 2026) TRUE TRUE AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `Art 96 the Commission` DOES `Art 96(2) update the guidelines previously adopted` AT 5
